From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: Alt+Tab's switcher and the desktop name card have a shadow

They ask for one (CS_DROPSHADOW), as Windows' have: sg-compositor's
sg-deskcomp draws it (winex11's _SG_SHADOW 2, 0744), and with its window
effects on they fade in and out like the other popups.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
@@ -1681,12 +1681,20 @@
     wc.hCursor = LoadCursorW( 0, (const WCHAR *)IDC_ARROW );
     wc.lpszClassName = L"SgTaskView";
     RegisterClassW( &wc );
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the desktop's name card and Alt+Tab's switcher ask
+     * for a shadow, as Windows' have one (drawn by sg-compositor's
+     * sg-deskcomp, see winex11's _SG_SHADOW) -- and fade in and out with
+     * its window effects */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NOSWITCHERSHADOW
+    wc.style = CS_DROPSHADOW;
+#endif
     wc.lpfnWndProc = osd_proc;
     wc.lpszClassName = L"SgVirtualDesktopOsd";
     RegisterClassW( &wc );
     wc.lpfnWndProc = switcher_proc;
     wc.lpszClassName = L"SgTaskSwitcher";
     RegisterClassW( &wc );
+    wc.style = 0;
     wc.lpfnWndProc = pager_proc;
     wc.lpszClassName = L"SgVirtualDesktopPager";
     RegisterClassW( &wc );
